<%/* Admin: external-service health.

     Today the page hosts a single Wasabi card. Future health cards
     (Archivematica, ArchivesSpace, curation-API filesystem) drop in
     as sibling content-card divs — each polled by its own HTMX
     trigger, each independent of the others so a slow probe can't
     starve the page.

     30s poll cadence: Wasabi config changes on the order of
     "someone edited .env and restarted curation-api" — much slower
     than the indexer's 5s. Keep it gentle. */%>
<h1 class="page-title">Services Health</h1>
<p class="page-subtitle">
    Reachability + auth probes for the external services the ingest
    pipeline depends on. Each card runs a single lightweight
    upstream check and refreshes on its own cadence.
</p>

<div class="content-card mb-3">
    <div class="content-card-header">
        <h2 style="font-size: 18px; margin: 0;">Wasabi S3</h2>
        <div class="control-group">
            <span class="htmx-indicator">
                <span class="spinner-border spinner-border-sm text-muted" role="status" aria-label="Loading"></span>
            </span>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div id="wasabi-status"
         hx-get="<%= dashboard_base %>/admin/services/wasabi"
         hx-trigger="load, every 30s"
         hx-swap="innerHTML">
        <div class="text-muted small p-3">Probing Wasabi…</div>
    </div>
</div>

<%/* Slot for future cards (Archivematica, ASpace, etc).
     Each new card is a fresh content-card div + its own HTMX
     poll. No JS changes needed. */%>
